{"title":"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e70d2995756450283c60e5ca45df746cda1ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5, x+\\frac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/0/130375b5e926048a5c6331d3e505e45d74e9cdb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+\\frac{2}{x} + \\frac{3}{x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" /> are multiplied, the product is a polynomial of degree.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94ea5462e8916afb8ca50879c0ccffe4df188b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 6\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 7\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"348\" height=\"17\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0febadd22013949e086a7580c27bf4816e48312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^5\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left(1+\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{3}{x^2}\\right) = (x^6+x^4)\\left(1+\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{3}{x^2}\\right) = x^6 + \\text{lower order terms}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"622\" height=\"45\" />, where we know that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed16c38e36fed49e600678cdfec693e8f45ff88e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^6$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> will not get cancelled out by e.g. a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc9829f903333c2f1f972cf4b17cca9bf0c4c67a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x^6$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> term since all the terms inside the brackets are positive. Thus the degree is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which is choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffc7368e8e7b77c88b0b4bf732c88c60e27b439.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME\" title=\"1983 AHSME\">1983 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems